From: MacVM validation <macvm@validation.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] reims: make Tahoe display capabilities self-consistent

Tahoe is the first guest in this validation path to consume device-info keys 37
and 44 and the negotiated floating-point physical dimensions. Advertise Apple9
consistently (Apple5..Apple9, not Apple10), use a 16:9 physical panel beside the
1920x1080 native mode, and populate both licensed dimension encodings.
---
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs         | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/drain/mod.rs  | 10 ++++--
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/drain/tests.rs | 27 +++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs
